# Real-user job: a Claude Code user wires an MCP server the way `claude mcp
# add <name> -- <command> [args]` does, then lists configured servers with
# a bare `mcp`. kiln has no `mcp add` subcommand today (`kiln mcp` only
# prints a read-only report), so the add is expected to fail and the
# server is expected to stay absent from /mcp and unusable by the model.
# This is a known gap the lead is closing; NOTE lines mark what should
# change once a Claude-Code-compatible `kiln mcp add` lands.
@real
@home scratch
@size 140x45
@setup mkdir -p {PROJ}/../bin && go -C {ROOT} build -o {PROJ}/../bin/incidents ./qa/fixtures/incident-mcp
@pre mcp add incidents -- {PROJ}/../bin/incidents
@pre mcp
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SHOT ready
WAIT 4
TYPE /mcp
KEY enter
SHOT mcp-dialog
EXPECT /incidents/
KEY esc
SHOT mcp-dialog-closed
TURN any open incidents?
SHOT answered
